  "how_to_verify": [
    "1. teamwork.py ledger verify   # recompute the sha256 chain over Ledger.jsonl",
    "2. compare the recomputed head hash with ledger.head above (a rebuilt or truncated ledger cannot reproduce it)",
    "3. sha256sum each artifact in this manifest",
    "4. git cat-file -t <git.head>   # the reviewed revision still exists",
    "5. teamwork.py trace <T-id|AC-id|P-id>   # follow any single claim",
    "note: artifacts are committed project output and are checkable by anyone; local_state is hidden working state, only checkable on the machine that produced it. Ledger.jsonl carries its own chain, so it is represented by ledger.head rather than a digest. docs/Team/Archive.md is append-only and gains an entry when a review passes, so it is not pinned as an artifact; follow its entries with `trace`."
  ]
